<html>
<title>Disk Support</title>
<body>

<h1>Disk Support</h1>

<p>
Disk support will be activated if the selected XML file includes a disk definition:
</p>
<ul>
<li><tt>ide</tt>: <tt>IDE</tt> GUI</li>
<li><tt>tu58</tt>: <tt>TU58</tt> GUI</li>
<li><tt>wd1770</tt>, <tt>wd1793</tt>: <tt>FDC</tt> GUI</li>
<li><tt>upd765</tt>: <tt>FDC</tt> or <tt>HD</tt> GUI</li>
</ul>


<h2>FDC GUI</h2>
<p>
<img src="images/disk_fdc.png" border="0" width="724" height="609">
</p>

<ul>
<li>(1) <strong>FDC x</strong> button</li>
<li>(2) <strong>File name</strong> text field</li>
<li>(3) <strong>Eject</strong> button</li>
</ul>

<p>
Depending on the configuration 1 to 4 drives (0-3) can be defined. In the example above a COMX is configured with 2 <tt>WD1770</tt> drives. To change a disk at runtime select a different file name using one of the <strong>FDC x</strong> buttons (1) or type a file name in the <strong>File name</strong> text field (2). To eject the disk use the <strong>Eject</strong> button (3) or remove the file name in the <strong>File name</strong> text field.
</p>


<h2>HD GUI</h2>
<p>
<img src="images/disk_hd.png" border="0" width="724" height="609">
</p>

<ul>
<li>(1) <strong>HD x</strong> button</li>
<li>(2) <strong>Double arrow</strong> button</li>
<li>(3) <strong>Directory</strong> text field</li>
</ul>

<p>
The <tt>HD</tt> GUI is available for <tt>upd765</tt> drives; instead of using a disk image, it supports direct access to the PC hard disk. The actual HD directory can be specified using the <strong>HD 0</strong> to <strong>HD 3</strong> buttons (1). The directory name will be displayed in the <strong>Directory</strong> text field (3).
</p>

<p>
To switch between <tt>HD</tt> and <tt>FDC</tt> mode, press one of the <strong>Double arrow</strong> buttons (2).
</p>

<p>
Using the <tt>HD</tt> feature allows for a simple import/export from/to the PC file system. Additionally, there is no disk size limit (310 KB for FDC images). In theory there is no limit to the total size of the directory; however, the following limitations still exist:
</p>

<ul>
<li>Maximum number of files in one directory is 128</li>
<li>Maximum file size is 300 KB to 310 KB depending on how many files are stored in the directory</li>
</ul>


<h2>IDE GUI</h2>
<p>
<img src="images/disk_ide.png" border="0" width="724" height="609">
</p>

<ul>
<li>(1) <strong>IDE x</strong> button</li>
<li>(2) <strong>File name</strong> text field</li>
<li>(3) <strong>Eject</strong> button</li>
</ul>

<p>
2 <tt>IDE</tt> drives (0 and 1) can be defined. In the example above a COSMAC Elf 2000 is configured. To change a disk at runtime select a different file name using one of the <strong>IDE x</strong> buttons (1) or type a file name in the <strong>File name</strong> text field (2). To eject the disk use the <strong>Eject</strong> button (3) or remove the file name in the <strong>File name</strong> text field.
</p>

<p>
After initial start-up, any file <tt>&lt;type&gt;-installation.ide</tt> (or <tt>&lt;type&gt;-installation.dsk</tt>) will be renamed to <tt>&lt;type&gt;.ide</tt> (or <tt>&lt;type&gt;.dsk</tt>) if that file does not exist.
</p>


<h2>TU58 GUI</h2>
<p>
<img src="images/disk_tu58.png" border="0" width="724" height="609">
</p>

<ul>
<li>(1) <strong>TU58 x</strong> button</li>
<li>(2) <strong>File name</strong> text field</li>
<li>(3) <strong>Eject</strong> button</li>
</ul>

<p>
2 <tt>TU58</tt> drives (0 and 1) can be defined. In the example above a SBC1802 is configured. To change a disk at runtime select a different file name using one of the <strong>TU58 x</strong> buttons (1) or type a file name in the <strong>File name</strong> text field (2). To eject the disk use the <strong>Eject</strong> button (3) or remove the file name in the <strong>File name</strong> text field.
</p>

</body>
</html>
